title: The Equality Bill Reaches Cabinet
subtitle: A ministry can draft a law; a coalition must still vote for it.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_government_card
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and equality_minister_party = "Lewica" and month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_equality_bill_timer <= 0 and minority_safety < 90
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_equality_bill_timer = 5
card-image: img/poland/deck_parliament.svg

= Equality

The dispute is over scope and timing.

- @full
- @employment
- @consult

@full
title: Table the full equality bill
subtitle: Requires the Equality Ministry.
choose-if: equality_minister_party = "Lewica"
unavailable-subtitle: Lewica does not control the ministry.
on-arrival: {!
const support = Number(Q.lgbt_equality_support);
const salience = Number(Q.lgbt_equality_salience);
const backlash = Number(Q.lgbt_equality_backlash);
const raw =
    (support - 50) / 15 + salience / 55 - backlash / 60;
const net = Math.round(Math.max(
    -3,
    Math.min(3, raw * (0.45 + salience / 100))
));
const scale = Math.max(0.65, Math.min(1.50, 1 + net * 0.15));
Q.progressive_credibility += Math.max(3, Math.round(7 * scale));
Q.feminist_trust += Math.max(3, Math.round(6 * scale));
Q.minority_safety += Math.max(2, Math.round(5 * scale));
Q.psl_coalition_dissent += Math.round(
    7 + salience / 25 + backlash / 35
);
Q.government_delivery += net >= 0 ? 3 : 2;
Q.public_trust += net * 0.45;
Q.left_poll += net * 0.10;
Q.lgbt_equality_support += net >= 1 ? 2 : (net <= -2 ? -1 : 1);
Q.lgbt_equality_salience += 8;
Q.lgbt_equality_backlash += net < 0 ? 6 : 3;
Q.card_public_response_score = net;
Q.card_public_response = net >= 2
    ? "breakthrough"
    : (net >= 1
        ? "favourable"
        : (net <= -2
            ? "reversal"
            : (net <= -1 ? "backlash" : "contested")));
Q.public_opinion_last_issue = "LGBT equality";
Q.public_opinion_last_reception = Q.card_public_response;
Q.public_opinion_last_delta = net;
Q.public_opinion_last_action = "Full equality bill";
Q.news_headline = net >= 1
    ? "The full equality bill reaches cabinet with public momentum"
    : (net <= -1
        ? "The equality bill reaches cabinet under a culture-war barrage"
        : "The full equality bill reaches cabinet");
!}

[? if card_public_response = "breakthrough": Cabinet expected a defensive
fight and instead finds a public majority asking why the law took so long.
Coalition conservatives still resist, but their veto is newly expensive. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "favourable": The proposal wins more approval
than alarm. PSL negotiators demand concessions without being able to claim the
country is behind them. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "contested": The bill mobilises supporters and
opponents in almost equal measure. Its fate now depends on coalition discipline
rather than an obvious public verdict. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "backlash": The rights case strengthens the
movement while high panic drives wavering voters toward procedural delay.
Coalition dissent rises faster than expected. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "reversal": A hostile, intensely polarised
climate makes the cabinet initiative an immediate electoral liability.
Withdrawal would cost the movement too. ?]

- #poland_card_finish

@employment
title: Begin with employment and hate-crime protections
subtitle: A smaller majority is available.
on-arrival: {!
const support = Math.min(100, Number(Q.lgbt_equality_support) + 9);
const salience = Number(Q.lgbt_equality_salience);
const backlash = Math.max(0, Number(Q.lgbt_equality_backlash) - 12);
const raw =
    (support - 50) / 15 + salience / 55 - backlash / 60;
const net = Math.round(Math.max(
    -3,
    Math.min(3, raw * (0.40 + salience / 110))
));
const scale = Math.max(0.70, Math.min(1.45, 1 + net * 0.14));
Q.progressive_credibility += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.minority_safety += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.psl_coalition_dissent += Math.max(
    1,
    Math.round(1 + Number(Q.lgbt_equality_backlash) / 45)
);
Q.government_delivery += 2;
Q.public_trust += net * 0.35;
Q.left_poll += net * 0.07;
Q.lgbt_equality_support += net >= 1 ? 1 : 0;
Q.lgbt_equality_salience += 4;
Q.lgbt_equality_backlash += net < 0 ? 2 : -1;
Q.card_public_response_score = net;
Q.card_public_response = net >= 2
    ? "breakthrough"
    : (net >= 1
        ? "favourable"
        : (net <= -2
            ? "reversal"
            : (net <= -1 ? "backlash" : "contested")));
Q.public_opinion_last_issue = "LGBT employment protections";
Q.public_opinion_last_reception = Q.card_public_response;
Q.public_opinion_last_delta = net;
Q.public_opinion_last_action = "Narrow equality package";
Q.news_headline = net >= 1
    ? "Employment protections find a working majority"
    : (net <= -1
        ? "Even the narrower equality package triggers a backlash"
        : "Cabinet advances a narrower equality package");
!}

[? if card_public_response = "breakthrough": The narrower bill reveals a much
larger practical majority than the coalition expected. Activists see a first
step; opponents struggle to make workplace protection sound radical. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "favourable": A limited package travels beyond
the progressive electorate and reduces the price of the next step. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "contested": The compromise secures votes but
does not settle whether incrementalism is persuasion or retreat. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "backlash": Even the limited bill is absorbed
into the wider culture war. The coalition gains fewer safe votes than promised.
?]
[? if card_public_response = "reversal": Public panic overwhelms the
incremental frame. The smaller bill pays nearly the full political price while
delivering less. ?]

- #poland_card_finish

@consult
title: Send the bill to public consultation
subtitle: Coalition peace now; movement impatience later.
on-arrival: {!
const salience = Number(Q.lgbt_equality_salience);
const backlash = Number(Q.lgbt_equality_backlash);
const delayScore = Math.round(Math.max(
    -3,
    Math.min(3, (backlash - salience) / 18)
));
Q.psl_coalition_dissent -= 3 + (delayScore > 0 ? 1 : 0);
Q.progressives_dissent += 4 + (delayScore < 0 ? 2 : 0);
Q.feminist_trust -= 2 + (delayScore < 0 ? 1 : 0);
Q.public_trust += delayScore * 0.30;
Q.left_poll += delayScore * 0.05;
Q.lgbt_equality_salience -= 3;
Q.lgbt_equality_backlash -= delayScore >= 0 ? 3 : 1;
Q.card_public_response_score = delayScore;
Q.card_public_response = delayScore >= 2
    ? "breakthrough"
    : (delayScore >= 1
        ? "favourable"
        : (delayScore <= -2
            ? "reversal"
            : (delayScore <= -1 ? "backlash" : "contested")));
Q.public_opinion_last_issue = "LGBT equality";
Q.public_opinion_last_reception = Q.card_public_response;
Q.public_opinion_last_delta = delayScore;
Q.public_opinion_last_action = "Equality-bill consultation";
Q.news_headline = delayScore >= 1
    ? "Consultation lowers the temperature around equality"
    : (delayScore <= -1
        ? "Consultation is heard as another equality delay"
        : "The equality bill enters consultation");
!}

[? if card_public_response = "favourable" or card_public_response = "breakthrough":
Backlash was running ahead of public attention. Consultation lowers the
temperature and gives cautious supporters a safer route into the argument. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "contested": Consultation buys coalition time
without changing the underlying balance. The movement starts counting days. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "backlash" or card_public_response = "reversal":
The issue is already salient enough that another process looks like avoidance.
Coalition peace is purchased with visible movement anger. ?]

- #poland_card_finish
